# $readBuild(pLibName) -> Character
# Reads the build number of ONE library out of its own $userinfo. It WRITES
# NOTHING - that is the whole difference to $bumpBuild, which is called only
# for a library a run really changed and therefore says nothing at all on a
# run that changed nothing. Two probe runs on 2026-09-06 carried no build
# line, and a protocol that cannot say which build produced it is worth less
# than one that can.
#
# Format read: EXEC-BUILD=<n> <stamp>  on its own line (see $bumpBuild).
# The sentinel guard is the same one and for the same reason: a $userinfo that
# is not character throws on the read, and a foreign structure is not ours to
# break.
#
# pLibName : char (param)   lib : ref   info : char   num p q : int
Set reference lib to $root.$libs.$findname(pLibName)
If isclear(lib)
	Quit method con('[build  ] ',pLibName,' is not open')
End If
Calculate info as '###UNREAD###'
Calculate info as lib.$userinfo
If info='###UNREAD###'
	Quit method con('[build  ] ',pLibName,' $userinfo is not character')
End If
Calculate p as pos('EXEC-BUILD=',info)
If p=0
	Quit method con('[build  ] ',pLibName,' carries no build number yet')
End If
Calculate q as pos(' ',mid(info,p+11))
If q=0
	Quit method con('[build  ] ',pLibName,' carries a malformed EXEC-BUILD tag')
End If
Calculate num as mid(info,p+11,q-1)
Quit method con('[build  ] ',pLibName,' at ',num)